      "problem": "$(-2)(3x+y)+8y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $(-2)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-2)(3x+y)+8y & = \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 3x+(-2)\\cdot y+8y & = \\\\ (-6x)+(-2y)+8y & = \\\\ -6x-2y+8y & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-6x-2y+8y & = \\\\ -6x+(8y-2y) & = \\\\ -6x+6y & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
