      "problem": "Simplify $4(2-a)+12.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $4$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2-a)+12 & = \\\\ 4\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-a)+12 & = \\\\ (8)+(-4a)+12 & = \\\\ 8-4a+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-4a+12 & = \\\\ (8+12)-4a & = \\\\ 20-4a\\end{aligned}\n$$",
