      "problem": "$12-3x+(4x-5)\\cdot 2=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $2$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-3x+(4x-5)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 12-3x+4x\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 12-3x+(8x)+(-10) & = \\\\ 12-3x+8x-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-3x+8x-10 & = \\\\ (12-10)+(-3x+8x) & = \\\\ (2)+(5x) & = \\\\ 2+5x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
